Summary of Position


The Customer Success Specialist (CSS) is responsible for supporting customer onboarding, product adoption, and long\-term customer satisfaction across assigned accounts. This role works closely with customers to ensure a positive experience, strengthen relationships, resolve issues, and help drive successful implementation and continued use of HR HealthCare’s products. The primary objective of the role is to improve customer outcomes, increase retention, and identify opportunities to expand value within the assigned market while supporting HR HealthCare’s purpose of Positively Impacting People’s Lives.




Duties \& Responsibilities


* Develop a strong understanding of HR HealthCare’s products, including use cases, features, benefits, and customer applications;
* Develop and maintain an understanding of customer workflows, operational needs, and the healthcare distribution environment to support successful implementation and adoption;
* Build and maintain strong relationships with customers, internal partners, and other key stakeholders to ensure a positive customer experience;
* Serve as a point of contact for assigned customers to support onboarding, product education, issue resolution, and ongoing account management;
* Conduct customer outreach through phone calls, e\-mails, and virtual meetings to support engagement, identify needs, and promote successful product usage;
* Partner with internal teams and external resources, as needed, to resolve customer concerns, coordinate implementation activities, and ensure timely follow\-through;
* Monitor customer health, product usage, and account activity to identify risks, opportunities, and areas for improvement;
* Leverage HR HealthCare’s customer and account data to identify adoption opportunities, support renewals, and strengthen customer relationships;
* Support the development and execution of customer success plans, including onboarding, training, and follow\-up activities;
* Utilize HR HealthCare’s CRM system to document all customer interactions, track account activity, and maintain accurate records;
* Support the Customer Success Manager and perform related duties as assigned;
* Adhere to all HR HealthCare policies and procedures and demonstrate understanding of HR HealthCare’s Values, Mission, and Vision;
* Demonstrate a positive, service\-oriented attitude and serve as a collaborative team player.


Skills/Requirements


* Bachelor’s degree preferred;
* 6 months to 1 year of experience in customer success, account management, healthcare support, sales, or a related field preferred;
* Experience in pharmaceutical, medical device, healthcare services, or related industries is a plus, but not required;
* Ability to learn and become proficient in HR HealthCare’s CRM and related customer support tools;
* Strong communication and relationship\-building skills with the ability to work effectively with internal and external stakeholders;
* Ability to multitask, take initiative, prioritize tasks, and manage time effectively;
* Demonstrated effectiveness working independently and in a team environment;
* Strong attention to detail and organizational skills;
* Excellent oral and written communication skills;

Overview:
**We’re not just a fashion brand \- we’re a movement.**  

At **GARAGE**, we live for unapologetic confidence, turning everyday moments into something unforgettable, and creating spaces where everyone can feel fearless. With **stores across North America** and a community that’s always growing, we’re looking for team players who want to make their mark. If you’re ready to bring the **energy**, **connect** with our community, and live **unapologetically** \- you belong here!  

Our core strengths are rooted in our team, our innovation and our customers. We are proud to hire and retain aspirational leaders who are driven to achieve great things and are recognized for their entrepreneurial spirit. **Job summary:**  

Reporting to the Store Manager, your role as Operations Associate is all about keeping the store flowing and the vibe strong. You’ll own the stockroom, keep inventory moving, process shipments, and make sure the floor stays full and fresh. From E\-comm orders to markdowns, you’ll help create a seamless experience that keeps our customers coming back. Behind the scenes, you’re the one making sure everything runs smoothly—an essential part of the team’s success. **Your role \& qualifications:*** High school diploma;
* 6\+ months of stockroom, inventory, or back\-of\-house retail experience (bonus if fashion\-related);
* Obsessed with details and keeping things organized;
* Proactive team player who takes ownership;
* Customer\-first mindset—you know your work powers the experience;
* Social media skills and tech\-savvy (mobile and computer skills are a plus);
* Having a flexible schedule (evenings, weekends, holidays).

**What we bring:*** Exclusive employee discount at Garage and Dynamite;
* Learning and development to help you level up;
* Employee referral program—bring your crew, get rewarded;
* A growing brand that invests in its people and their future.
* A competitive base salary. Compensation may vary based on skills and experience.
* 401(K)\- eligibility rules may apply based on laws and regulations.

 **Our promise…**  

We’re all about growth, energy, and community. Join us and be part of something bigger than retail—be part of the movement. **A little bit about how we hire…**  

We are committed to employment equity and making the application process as fair and efficient as possible! To handle the volume of applications, we use an Artificial Intelligence\-assisted tool to help us sort and evaluate applications for this role. This tool gives us a helpful starting point, but it never makes a final hiring decision on its own. Our hiring team always reviews the information to decide who moves forward.  

In compliance with applicable federal, state, and local laws, this tool is reviewed regularly to ensure it does not produce biased or discriminatory outcomes. Where required, it also undergoes an independent annual bias audit, and a summary of the most recent audit will be made publicly available. **Candidates that are retained will be contacted for an interview.**  

\#LI\-DNP  

\#LI\-Onsite

